{#
  Who wrote a person's prose, and whether it publishes.

  33 person records carry a body and an author bio that came in from the old
  WordPress site. The text is written narrative with no citations and no
  established author, and nothing on the record said so, which meant a reader
  had no way to tell it from the archive's own legacy writing. The
  bodyAuthorship field says; this macro is the single place that decides what
  that means for the front end.

  Publishes: legacy-leon, editorial-2026.
  Does not:  wordpress-import-unsourced, mixed, and empty.

  Empty does not publish on purpose. An unclassified body is one nobody has
  looked at, and silence is not a claim that the text is sound. The same
  applies when the field does not exist yet: before it is applied, every person
  body is the WordPress import, so the honest default is to hold it back.

  The prose is not deleted and not touched. It stays in the database and in the
  control panel, where it is the starting point for the editorial profile that
  will replace it.

  Prints '1' for publishes and nothing otherwise, so callers test it with
  |trim. Used by persons/_entry.twig, articles/_entry.twig (the author box) and
  _partials/head/meta.twig (the description and the social cards).
#}
{% macro publishes(entry) %}
  {%- set has = false -%}
  {%- for f in entry.fieldLayout.customFields -%}
    {%- if f.handle == 'bodyAuthorship' %}{% set has = true %}{% endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
  {%- if has and entry.bodyAuthorship in ['legacy-leon', 'editorial-2026'] %}1{% endif -%}
{% endmacro %}
